title: The Retirement of DuFour
subtitle: The President steps down...
new-page: true
view-if: year = 1934 and month >= 7 and president = "DuFour" and not gnu_formed and not dufour_assassinated
on-arrival: {!
Q.round = 0;
Q.dufour_dead = 1;

Q.lib_running = 1;
Q.center_running = 1;
Q.reactionary_running = 1;
Q.hamster_running = 0;

Q.gessler_run_1934 = 1;
Q.heuss_run_1934 = 0;
Q.adenauer_run_1934 = 1;
Q.bruning_run_1934 = 0;
Q.seldte_run_1934 = 1;
Q.hergt_run_1934 = 0;
Q.lettow_vorbeck_run_1934 = 0;
Q.hugenberg_run_1934 = 0;

Q.president = "Burnell (acting)";
if (Q.judicial_reform >= 4) Q.president = "Grothmoor (acting)";

Q.reactionary_candidate_1934 = "Selden";
Q.reactionary_candidate_1934_disp = "Roderick Selden";
Q.lib_candidate_1934 = "Gesling";
Q.lib_candidate_1934_disp = "Gareth Gesling";
Q.center_candidate_1934 = "Aldermoor";
Q.center_candidate_1934_disp = "Konrad Aldermoor";

Q.marcher_candidate = "Eckhart";
Q.collectivist_candidate = "Halsmark";
Q.royalist_candidate = "Gallax";

if (Q.collectivist_leader === "Conciliators") Q.collectivist_candidate = "Munzer";
if (Q.gallax_deported || !Q.gallax_citizen || Q.gallax_dead) Q.royalist_candidate = "Gorrick";
if ((Q.ddp_ideology == "Left" || Q.ddp_ideology == "Moderate" && Q.pro_republic >= 75) && !Q.lvp_formed || (Q.lvp_ideology != "Right" && Q.pro_republic >= 75 || Q.lvp_leader == "Hewes") && Q.lvp_formed && Q.lvp_votes >= 10) {
    Q.heuss_run_1934 = 1;
    Q.gessler_run_1934 = 0;
    Q.lib_candidate_1934 = "Hewes";
    Q.lib_candidate_1934_disp = "Theodor Hewes";
}

if (Q.concord_formed) {
    Q.reactionary_candidate_1934 = "Lettow_Vorbeck";
    Q.reactionary_candidate_1934_disp = "Paul von Lettow_Vorbeck";
    Q.lettow_vorbeck_run_1934 = 1;

    Q.center_running = 0;
    Q.seldte_run_1934 = 0;
    Q.hugenberg_run_1934 = 1;
    Q.adenauer_run_1934 = 0;
    Q.hamster_running = 1;
    Q.dnf_candidate = "Mallin";
}

if (Q.traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate" && !Q.concord_formed) {
    Q.seldte_run_1934 = 0;
    Q.hergt_run_1934 = 1;
    if (Q.dnf_votes >= 6) {
        Q.hugenberg_run_1934 = 1;
        Q.dnf_candidate = "Mallin";
    } else {
        Q.dnf_candidate = Q.royalist_candidate;
    }
    Q.reactionary_candidate_1934 = "Hargen";
    Q.reactionary_candidate_1934_disp = "Cuthbert Hargen";
}

if (Q.lautenbach_adopted && !Q.concord_formed) {
    Q.center_candidate_1934 = "Askew";
    Q.center_candidate_1934_disp = "Edmund Askew";
    Q.bruning_run_1934 = 1;
    Q.adenauer_run_1934 = 0;
    Q.lib_running = 0;
}

if (Q.lib_running) {
    Q.ddp_candidate = Q.lib_candidate_1934;
    Q.lvp_candidate = Q.lib_candidate_1934;
    Q.gold_candidate = Q.lib_candidate_1934;
} else {
    Q.ddp_candidate = Q.center_candidate_1934;
    Q.lvp_candidate = Q.center_candidate_1934;
    Q.gold_candidate = Q.center_candidate_1934;
}

Q.unionist_candidate = Q.center_candidate_1934;
if (Q.concord_formed) Q.unionist_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate_1934;

Q.traditionalist_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate_1934;
Q.other_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate_1934;

Q.kvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate_1934;
if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1934 == "Selden" && (Q.center_candidate_1934 == "Askew" || Q.pro_republic >= 70)) {
    Q.kvp_candidate = Q.center_candidate_1934;
    Q.kvp_wholesome = 1;
}

Q.sapd_candidate = Q.collectivist_candidate;

if (Q.reactionary_candidate_1934 == "Lettow_Vorbeck") Q.reactionary_candidate_1934 = "Lethmoor";

Q.is_unity_candidate = 0;

// DuFour's retirement endorsement -- a thumb on the scale, graded by commonwealth_standing.
// middling/recovered (>= 50) -> the democratic bloc; low (< 50, pre-Rubicon) -> Traditionalist + Unionist.
// Never a Royalist (Rubicon uncrossed) or a Collectivist.
if (Q.commonwealth_standing >= 50) {
    Q.dufour_endorses = "democrats";
    Q.Liberal_bonus = (Q.Liberal_bonus || 0) + 2.5;
    Q.Center_bonus = (Q.Center_bonus || 0) + 2.5;
    Q.Eckhart_bonus = (Q.Eckhart_bonus || 0) + 2.5;
} else {
    Q.dufour_endorses = "right";
    Q.Reactionary_bonus = (Q.Reactionary_bonus || 0) + 3;
    Q.Center_bonus = (Q.Center_bonus || 0) + 2.5;
}
!}
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/DuFour_head.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
tags: event

= The Retirement of DuFour

President DuFour has announced his retirement, stepping down to care for his family after long years at the republic's helm. An era of history is closing, and the future remains to be seen.

The nation pays tribute to its war hero and outgoing president, with even some warmth among committed <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">icans</span> and <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>. After all, DuFour steered the republic through some of its most challenging times, without giving in to extremists on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>. Perhaps he is one reason democracy remains alive.

[? if dufour_endorses == "democrats": On his way out, DuFour has lent his considerable prestige to the Commonwealth's democratic candidates, urging the nation to entrust the republic to steady, constitutional hands. ?][? if dufour_endorses == "right": On his way out, DuFour — his patience with the republic's endless squabbles worn thin — has thrown his weight behind the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">Traditionalists</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>, the firm, orderly hands he now trusts to hold the realm together. ?]

New presidential elections are to be held as soon as possible. The Commonwealth political landscape is wide open, with contenders from all over the political space. In the meantime, Supreme Court chief justice [? if judicial_reform < 4 : Erwin Burnell ?][? if judicial_reform >= 4 : Gorman Grothmoor ?] serves as the acting president.

# Gorman Grothmoor is the supreme court chief justice in judicial reform.

- @candidates: Who are the candidates so far?

@candidates
go-to: candidate_menu

[? if not gallax_deported and gallax_citizen and not gallax_dead : Of course, Alaric Gallax will be running for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>, in his third run. We have kept him out of power so far, but nothing is certain. ?]

[? if gallax_deported or gallax_dead or (not gallax_citizen and not gallax_deported and not gallax_dead) : With Gallax out of the picture, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> will be running Ulric Gorrick as their candidate. ?]
This might be the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>' last hurrah; the party's internal contradictions are heightening, and it is in desperate shortage of funds.

[? if seldte_run_1934: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> will nominate Roderick Selden, leader of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> paramilitary group. He will be endorsed by many of DuFour's most right-wing supporters. They are working more closely with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> than before, and in the second round, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> parties are expected to consolidate into a single anti-<span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> front. [? if kvp_formed and kvp_candidate == center_candidate_1934: However, the <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>, feeling alienated by this arrangement, has decided to support whomever the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] puts forth. ?] ?][? if hergt_run_1934: The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> will nominate Cuthbert Hargen,[? if traditionalist_leader != "Hargen":&nbsp;former?] leader of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> and former vice chancellor. He will be endorsed by many of DuFour's most right-wing supporters. They are working more closely with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> than before, and in the second round, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> parties are expected to consolidate into a single anti-<span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> front. ?][? if concord_formed: The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> has come together in full support of nominating General Lethmoor, a war hero who was once a member of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. Despite his initial reluctance, the popular general has agreed to their nomination, signaling his intent to uphold the legacy of DuFour. ?]

[? if not seldte_run_1934: Alfred Mallin is dissatisfied with endorsing [+ reactionary_candidate_1934 +] and prefers to run himself. However, his finances have been crippled by having solely financed the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>?] throughout the economic depression, which has also eroded the income from his media empire. [? if hugenberg_run_1934: Despite this, he has scraped together what remains of his personal fortune to launch a presidential campaign, hoping to leverage a second-round endorsement for concessions from [+ reactionary_candidate_1934 +]. ?][? if not hugenberg_run_1934: In an effort to preserve both his party’s solvency and what remains of his wealth, he has refrained from running or endorsing anyone—much to the frustration of his colleagues. ?] ?]

[? if collectivist_leader = "Conciliators" : Given the failure of Halsmark's previous runs for president, and his declining stature in the party, the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> will be running Willi Munzer, a controversial figure sometimes called the "Red millionaire". He is a media magnate who leads a number of <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> front organizations. ?]
[? if collectivist_leader != "Conciliators" : This will be Ernst Halsmark's third run for president as leader of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>. Despite his previous electoral defeats, he retains the loyalty of the party as well as <span style="color: #8B0000;">Halsmark</span>'s <span style="color: #750e0e;">Central Union</span>. ?]

[? if not concord_formed: Many <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">icans</span> of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], and <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> float the idea of running Hugo Eckhart, a nationally renowed Zeppelin captain, as a unity candidate. While he has some nationalistic views, he is also ardently opposed to <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Imperial Sovereigntism</span>. ?]

[? if not concord_formed: Barring that, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] are planning to run separate candidates in the first round if the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> runs its own candidate. [? if adenauer_run_1934: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is considering nominating Konrad Aldermoor, mayor of Köln and member of the Heartland state legislature. He calls for an alliance of conservative Christian democrats that encompasses both Catholics and Protestants.?][? if bruning_run_1934: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is considering nominating Edmund Askew, their former Chancellor, known for his popular and successful public works program. Widely credited with reviving the Commonwealth’s economy, he is expected to receive broad support from the propertied parties that participated in his government should he choose to run. ?]?] [? if ddp_candidate == "Gesling": The [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] might nominate Gareth Gesling, former defense minister, who has crossover appeal to conservatives[? if gold_exist and not lvp_formed:&nbsp;in the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] and other parties who dislike the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> front. ?][? if ddp_candidate == "Hewes": The [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] might nominate Theodor Hewes, a prominent left-liberal journalist, who presents a strong defense of the Unity Republic and its democratic institutions. He aims to be the candidate for the young generation, and propertied <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">cans</span>. ?]

As for the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, we could support a joint [? if not concord_formed: Unity?][? if concord_formed: <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] ?] Coalition candidate or run our own.
[? if braun_campaign : Lyle Bristol is tired. He ran and failed in the previous two presidential elections, and no longer wishes to run. His wife is ill enough that he wishes to stay by her side. ?][? if braun_campaign = 0 and not marcher_heartland: Lyle Bristol is tired. After being deposed in Heartland, he has largely retired from politics, and is devoting his time to caring for his dying wife. ?][? if braun_campaign = 0 and marcher_heartland : Lyle Bristol is tired. He does not wish to run, but he is willing to be convinced that he is needed at this moment. His wife is terminally ill, and he does not want more responsibilities. ?]
Kurt Shackley is an ambitious rising star in the party, and would be all too willing to run. He was a hero in the Great War, but his relatively young age might be relevant.
[? if womens_rights >= 6 and family_law >= 2 and womens_work >= 2 and welfare > 0: Or, perhaps it is time for a woman to become president. the Commonwealth and the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> have been leading on women's rights for years, and it is only fitting that we should elect the world's first female president. Perhaps Marie Jessamy could be seen as the "mother of the nation" for her work in social welfare. However, her divorce 28 years ago might make it difficult for the Catholics to support her. ?]

[? if presidential_powers >= 1 and pro_republic >= 60 and pacifism >= 3: Since the Commonwealth has been largely democratized and presidential powers reduced, we can also support another non-traditional political figure, someone from the cultural, scientific, or literary spheres. They will perhaps be the symbol of a new the Commonwealth that has moved beyond its past. ?]

@candidate_menu

- @eckener_r1: Support Hugo Eckhart as a joint Unity Coalition candidate.
- @adenauer_r1: Support [+ center_candidate_1934_disp +] of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].
- @gessler_r1: Support [+ lib_candidate_1934_disp +] of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?].
- @thalmann_r1: Support Ernst Halsmark of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
- @munzenberg_r1: Support Willi Munzer of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
- @braun_r1: Support Lyle Bristol.
- @schumacher_r1: Support Kurt Shackley.
- @juchacz_r1: Support Marie Jessamy.
- @cultural_figure: Support a nonpartisan cultural figure?

@eckener_r1
subtitle: -1 resource - After nominating him, we still have to convince the other parties to support him.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 1 : -1 resource - Not enough resources. ?]
view-if: not concord_formed
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Eckhart"; is_unity_candidate = 1
go-to: r1_menu

We have convinced Hugo Eckhart to run on behalf of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and hopefully the rest of the Unity Coalition as well.


@adenauer_r1
view-if: center_running
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = center_candidate_1934; unionist_relation += 4; Center_bonus -= 2.5 if ((unionist_relation < 40 and reactionary_candidate_1934 == "Selden") or (unionist_relation < 55 and reactionary_candidate_1934 != "Selden")) and reactionary_running; Reactionary_bonus += 2.5 if ((unionist_relation < 40 and reactionary_candidate_1934 == "Selden") or (unionist_relation < 55 and reactionary_candidate_1934 != "Selden")) and reactionary_running; is_unity_candidate = 1; kvp_candidate = traditionalist_candidate
go-to: r1_menu

We have endorsed [+ center_candidate_1934_disp +] of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?].

[? if unionist_relation < 40 : With our support of [+ center_candidate_1934 +], some of the most conservative parts of the <span style="color: #A2D8E0;">the Arcanists</span> have broken away from the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], shifting their support to the [? if reactionary_candidate_1934 == "Selden": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> leader?][? if reactionary_candidate_1934 != "Selden": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> ?] [+ reactionary_candidate_1934 +]. Hopefully it doesn't lead to a repeat of the 4290 Presidential election. ?][? if kvp_formed and kvp_wholesome: The <span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span> will now be supporting [+ kvp_candidate +].  ?]

@gessler_r1
view-if: lib_running
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = lib_candidate_1934; ddp_relation += 4; lvp_relation += 4; gold_candidate = reactionary_candidate_1934 if gold_relation < 40 and not lvp_formed and gold_exist; is_unity_candidate = 1
go-to: r1_menu

[? if gessler_run_1934: We have endorsed Gareth Gesling, independent formerly of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**Golds**</span>. ?][? if heuss_run_1934: We have endorsed Theodor Hewes of the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]. ?]

[? if gold_relation < 40 and not lvp_formed and gold_exist : With our support of [+ lib_candidate_1934 +], the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> components supporting him have broken away and are now shifting their support to [+ reactionary_candidate_1934 +]. ?]

@thalmann_r1
view-if: collectivist_candidate = "Halsmark" 
choose-if: collectivist_relation >= 50 and reformist_strength < left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if collectivist_relation < 50 : We do not have good enough relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span>, so they are not even willing to accept our support. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength : The reformist faction is able to dissuade the party from supporting this arrangement. ?]

Supporting Halsmark is rather unpopular in our party, even if the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> accept our support. Are we sure?

- @support_thalmann_2: Yes, we will support Halsmark, despite the reformists' pleas against it.
- @candidate_menu: Who else can we support?

@support_thalmann_2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Halsmark"; collectivist_relation += 5; reformist_dissent += 10; center_dissent += 6; labor_dissent += 5; knight_dissent += 10; faithful_marcher -= 5; burgher_marcher -= 5; guild_marcher -= 5; landed_marcher -= 5; ddp_relation -= 8; lvp_relation -= 12; gold_relation -= 15; unionist_relation -= 10; communist_coalition += 2; is_unity_candidate = 0
go-to: r1_menu

Fine. We have endorsed Ernst Halsmark of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> for president.


@munzenberg_r1
subtitle: Supporting Munzer is unpopular among the reformists, but less so than Halsmark would've been.
view-if: collectivist_candidate = "Munzer" 
choose-if: collectivist_relation >= 40 and reformist_strength < left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if collectivist_relation < 40 : We do not have good enough relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span>, so they are not even willing to accept our support. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength : The reformist faction is able to dissuade the party from supporting this arrangement. ?]
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Munzer"; collectivist_relation += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; ddp_relation -= 4; gold_relation -= 8; lvp_relation -= 8; unionist_relation -= 6; is_unity_candidate = 0
go-to: r1_menu

We have endorsed Willi Munzer of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.


@braun_r1
subtitle: -2 resources.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2 : -2 resources - Not enough resources. ?][? if braun_campaign != 0 or not marcher_heartland : Bristol no longer wants to run. ?]
choose-if: braun_campaign = 0 and marcher_heartland and resources >= 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Bristol"; resources -= 2; is_unity_candidate = 0
go-to: r1_menu

We have convinced Lyle Bristol to run for president once more.


@schumacher_r1
subtitle: -2 resources.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2 : -2 resources - Not enough resources. ?]
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Shackley"; resources -= 2; is_unity_candidate = 0
go-to: r1_menu

We have nominated Kurt Shackley to be our presidential candidate.


@juchacz_r1
subtitle: -2 resources.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 2 : -2 resources - Not enough resources. ?]
view-if: womens_rights >= 6 and family_law >= 2 and womens_work >= 2 and welfare > 0
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Jessamy"; resources -= 2; is_unity_candidate = 0
go-to: r1_menu

We have nominated Marie Jessamy as our presidential candidate, the first woman ever to be nominated for this position!

@cultural_figure
subtitle: The next president should be a symbol of the new the Commonwealth...
view-if: presidential_powers >= 1 and pro_republic >= 60 and pacifism >= 3

Since the presidency has been made a largely ceremonial figure by our reforms, we might set a precedent by nominating a nonpartisan pro-democracy figure from the cultural, scientific, or literary worlds. There are many potential candidates...

- @einstein_r1: Aldous Verrin, physicist.
- @mann_r1: Aldric Mann, left-wing writer.
- @ossietzky_r1: Carl von Ostwick, pacifist journalist.
- @candidate_menu: Actually, we should nominate someone else.

@einstein_r1
subtitle: -2 resources
view-if: science >= 2 and kwg_research >= 1 and (major_curriculum = "scientific" or minor_curriculum = "scientific")
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Verrin"; ddp_candidate = "Verrin"; resources -= 2; is_unity_candidate = 0; is_cultural_candidate = 1;
go-to: r1_menu

Aldous Verrin is a Nobel Prize-winning scientist, director of the Reikzar Institute for Physics, and international advocate for peace. He was a founding member of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Commonwealth Democratic Party</span> ([? if dstp_formed: whose successor would support him in the election?][? if not dstp_formed: who will support him in the election?]), but has also expressed sympathy towards <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span>.

He did not wish to run for president, disliking the public nature of campaigning, but we have somehow convinced him that his candidacy will be crucial to the future of the Commonwealth and the world. As a <span style="color: #005EB8;">Jewish</span> Commonwealth pacifist, his becoming president would be a repudiation of everything the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> stand for.

The <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> will endorse Verrin's candidacy.

@mann_r1
subtitle: -2 resources - He might be too <span style="color: #700000;">far left</span> for the propertied parties.
view-if: collectivist_relation >= 50
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Mann"; resources -= 2; is_unity_candidate = 0; is_cultural_candidate = 1;
go-to: r1_menu

Aldric Mann is a world-renowned novelist and poet who is also known to be a left-wing activist. His political sympathy lies with the <span style="color: #700000;">far left</span>, and he supported the revolutions in 4283 and 4284. He has long lived in the shadow of his better-known brother, Thomas Mann.

Mann is willing to accept the nomination for president.


@ossietzky_r1
view-if: weltbuhne_dropped = 1
subtitle: -2 resources - He might be too <span style="color: #700000;">far left</span> for the propertied parties.
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: marcher_candidate = "Ostwick"; resources -= 2; is_unity_candidate = 0; is_cultural_candidate = 1;
go-to: r1_menu

Carl von Ostwick is a left-wing journalist who is the publisher of the Brocksby, a news magazine. He is most known for exposing the secret Commonwealth rearmament program in 4294, which brought him international renown. In the 4297 presidential election, he endorsed the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> Halsmark.

Ostwick is extremely reluctant to become a politician, and has been an iconoclastic figure his entire life, criticizing the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> as being part of the establishment. It is with a sense of irony that he accepts our nomination.


