@seldte_victory
on-arrival: chancellor = "Gallax"; chancellor_party = "Royalist"; gallax_revive = 1 if gallax_dead

With Selden's victory, the balance of power passes to the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>. [? if gallax_deported: His first act is to depose the current chancellor and appoint Alaric Gallax as chancellor, first undoing his deportation. ?][? if not gallax_deported: His first act is to depose the current chancellor and appoint Alaric Gallax as chancellor. ?] [? if gallax_dead: It turns out Gallax never actually died—he faked his suicide. With no body ever recovered, allegedly cremated beyond recognition, he instead fled to the Allied States and lived under the alias "Phelan Hilt," working as a painter. Now, he is being called back. ?]

- @hitler_takes_power: What next?
- @hitler_constitutional: This is blatantly unconstitutional!

@hergt_victory_nazi
on-arrival: chancellor = "Selden"; chancellor_party = "Traditionalist"

With Hargen’s victory—secured with the support of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>—the balance of power shifts to them under the terms of their deal. However, Hargen remains deeply reluctant to appoint Alaric Gallax as chancellor[? if not gallax_citizen or gallax_deported:—which would require granting him Commonwealth citizenship?]. Instead, he names <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> leader Roderick Selden as a compromise candidate between the two parties. Selden will govern through presidential decree, leading a <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> cabinet.

- @seldte_takes_power: What next?
- @seldte_constitutional: This is blatantly unconstitutional!

@hergt_victory_lite

With Hargen’s victory—and without having relied on <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> support—he is under no obligation to appoint [+ royalist_candidate +] as chancellor. A committed <span style="color: #808080;">monarchist</span>, Hargen is expected to pursue steps toward restoring the Hohenzollerns. Unlike DuFour, he is far more openly partisan and intends to exclude the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> from government throughout his seven-year term.

@lettow_vorbeck_victory

Unfortunately, Paul von Lethmoor, a <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalist</span> not far different from DuFour, has been elected president. A return to government under his leadership—his Camarilla certainly won’t allow it. Let’s hope his personal disdain for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> keeps them from ever entering government.

@seldte_constitutional
view-if: presidential_powers

We have passed a constitutional amendment preventing the president from having the power to arbitrarily dismiss a government. To undo this, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> has called a plebiscite on a new constitutional amendment. Stormtroopers are in the streets, "convincing" voters to support their proposal. the Commonwealth is nearing civil war.

- @fight: We will fight the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span> in the streets!
- @defeat_democratic: We can only defeat the Sovereigntists through democratic means!

@hitler_constitutional
view-if: presidential_powers

We have passed a constitutional amendment preventing the president from having the power to arbitrarily dismiss a government. To undo this, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> has called a plebiscite on a new constitutional amendment. Stormtroopers are in the streets, "convincing" voters to support their proposal. the Commonwealth is nearing civil war.

- @fight: We will fight the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span> in the streets!
- @defeat_democratic: We can only defeat the Sovereigntists through democratic means!

@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @defeat_democratic: It is not too late to fight constitutionally.

@defeat_democratic
on-arrival: {!
Q.pro_democracy_votes = Q.marcher_votes + Q.ddp_votes + (Q.lvp_votes / 2) + Q.unionist_votes - (Q.loyalist_strength*Q.loyalist_militancy/10) + (Q.banner_strength*Q.banner_militancy/10);
if (Q.pro_republic >= 60) {
    Q.pro_democracy_votes += Q.collectivist_votes;
    Q.pro_democracy_votes += Q.gold_votes;
    Q.pro_democracy_votes += (Q.lvp_votes / 2);
}
!}
go-to: ref_win if pro_democracy_votes >= 50; ref_lose if pro_democracy_votes < 50

@ref_win
on-arrival: constitutional_crisis = 1

Despite the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> threats, supporters of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and the democratic parties refuse to turn out for the referendum, depriving it of the necessary threshold to pass. This is a small victory, as stormtroopers still run rampant in the streets. There is no constitutional path to absolute power, but will that stop the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>? 

- @game_over: The ending is yet to be seen...

@ref_lose

- @seldte_takes_power: What next?
- @hitler_takes_power: What next?


@election_end
go-to: eckener_win if winner = "Eckhart"; juchacz_win if winner = "Jessamy"; bundesrepublik_win if winner = "Shackley" or winner = "Aldermoor"; hitler_victory if winner = "Gallax" or winner = "Gorrick" or winner = "Gorrick"; seldte_victory if winner = "Selden"; hergt_victory_nazi if winner = "Hargen" and royalist_candidate == "Hargen"; hergt_victory_lite if winner = "Hargen" and royalist_candidate != "Hargen"; lettow_vorbeck_victory if winner = "Lethmoor"; munzenberg_victory if winner = "Munzenberg" or winner = "Munzer"; thalmann_victory if winner = "Halsmark" or winner = "Halsmark"; nazis_lose if winner = "Bristol" or winner = "Gesling" or winner = "Hewes" or winner = "Askew"; cultural_victory if winner = "Ostwick" or winner = "Mann"; einstein_victory if winner = "Verrin"
on-arrival: {!
Q.president = Q.winner;
if (Q.president == "Askew") Q.president = "Askew";
if (Q.president == "Halsmark") Q.president = "Halsmark";
if (Q.president == "Munzenberg") Q.president = "Munzer";
if (Q.president == "Gorrick") Q.president = "Gorrick";

if (Q.president == "Halsmark" || Q.president == "Munzer" || Q.president == "Shackley" || Q.president == "Vesh" || Q.president == "Grenshaw" || Q.president == "Jessamy" || Q.president == "Bristol" || Q.president == "Ostwick" || Q.president == "Mann" || Q.president == "Verrin") {
    Q.president_ideology = "Left";
} else if (Q.president == "Eckhart" || Q.president == "Aldermoor" || Q.president == "Askew" || Q.president == "Gesling" || Q.president == "Hewes") {
    Q.president_ideology = "Moderate";
} else {
    Q.president_ideology = "Right";
}
!}

The election has been won by [+ winner_desc +].

@thalmann_victory
go-to:  thalmann_victory_2 if rubicon and (dynamic_mode or historical_mode or difficulty == 1); thalmann_democrat if presidential_powers and (not rubicon or not (dynamic_mode or historical_mode or difficulty == 1)); thalmann_civil_war if not presidential_powers and (not rubicon or not (dynamic_mode or historical_mode or difficulty == 1))

@thalmann_victory_2
go-to: thalmann_democrat if presidential_powers; thalmann_civil_war if not presidential_powers
achievement: nach_schleicher_wir

@thalmann_civil_war
on-arrival: collectivist_relation = 80

# TODO: depose the chancellor?

Halsmark wastes no time in consolidating power, using all means available to reshape the government. In response, the far-right immediately launches a coup attempt. We have no choice but to unite with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span>...

- @civil_war: This is civil war.

@thalmann_democrat

Despite the victory of the anti-constitutionalist Halsmark, he appears to be respecting the constitutional constraints on presidential power, at least for now. There is no appetite on the right for a coup at this moment. The Burghers have to live with a <span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span> president, at least for now.


@munzenberg_victory
achievement: rote_millionar
go-to: nazis_lose if not rubicon; nach_schleicher_wir if rubicon

The propertied and right-wing parties are up in arms about the prospect of a <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> president, although Munzer and the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> conciliators take pains to assure the Commonwealth of their commitment to the democratic republic. There is no energy for a coup against the new president. The Burghers will have to live with whatever comes.

